# build_apps.py writes LayerTrack.html and BroodTrack.html with LF endings and
# then compares them byte-for-byte. With core.autocrlf=true (the Windows
# default, and what this machine is set to) a fresh checkout would hand them
# back as CRLF, so every build would look like a full-file rewrite and
# `build_apps.py --check` would never pass. Pin the whole repo to LF; every
# file committed so far already is.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Not text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.xlsx binary
